{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":5,"timestamp":1781877610,"nonce":"g5H6+GlL3xBhrFQdf1HvAe9N5kY=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABGDfNIs8AAAAGRvZ5xw"},"added":["bug"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"timestamp":1781919194,"nonce":"1SLWLLNY2IUY7wrRp8KUdqWBd84=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABG3l7zQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/300#issuecomment-4755913677"},"message":"**Not reproducible — the starboard frame was present and resolvable in the deployment bag; no URDF change needed.**\n\nI traced this end-to-end against the exact bag (`gabby/logs/bizzyboat_sonar/2026-06-16T14-17-37+00-00`). Three independent checks all show the starboard TF was fine:\n\n1. **Source (already correct, since #237 / 2026-06-08).** `bizzyboat_project11/urdf/sensors/sidescan.xacro` defines `_port`, `_starboard`, and `_down` symmetrically, and the `garmin_sidescan` driver stamps `bizzy/garmin_sidescan_starboard` (`FRAME_SUFFIX['stbd']='starboard'`, base `frame_id` `bizzy/garmin_sidescan`). Names match exactly. Port and starboard were added in the *same* commit, so a stale build would have dropped port too.\n2. **Deployed bag.** The recorded `/bizzy/robot_description` contains all four sidescan frames; `/tf_static` contains `bizzy/garmin_sidescan → bizzy/garmin_sidescan_starboard`; starboard pings are stamped `bizzy/garmin_sidescan_starboard` (52005 of them). Replaying the bag's TF into a buffer, `earth → …_starboard` resolves **201/201** sampled pings across the whole run — identical to port and down.\n3. **Live mosaicker.** Running `marine_sidescan_mosaic` (sim-time) against this bag produces **zero** `no usable earth→…_starboard transform` warnings and writes tiles continuously.\n\nThe error originates in `marine_sidescan_mosaic/src/mosaic_node.cpp:288`, whose `lookupPose()` is side-agnostic — port and starboard share the identical `lookupTransform(earth, msg.header.frame_id, …)` path. Given both frames resolve, there's no code path where starboard fails but port succeeds. The original observation was most likely a transient at first run (node started mid-replay missing the transient-local `/tf_static` window, or a `use_sim_time` / tf-buffer warm-up gap), surfaced through the throttled warning and misread as a systematic, starboard-only, missing-frame failure.\n\n**Recommendation:** closing as not-a-bug for the BizzyBoat platform. If a genuine intermittent drop resurfaces in the live mosaicker, it should be chased in unh_marine_autonomy#173 (startup/tf-warm-up handling), not the URDF.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":4,"timestamp":1781919195,"nonce":"MNP6731g2qfEt99WK2s/JSNfxDM=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABGDfNIs8AAAAGSADYkQ"},"status":2}]}